---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Privacy Policy — Free QR Code Generator" 
  description="Comprehensive Privacy Policy for freeqrcode-generator.com covering client-side zero-storage architecture, GDPR, CCPA, cookie disclosure, dynamic QR telemetry, and data retention standards."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-12 shadow-card space-y-10">
      
      <!-- Document Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6 space-y-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">Legal Documentation</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-slate-500 pt-1 font-mono">
          <span>Effective Date: August 27, 2026</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Domain: freeqrcode-generator.com</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Version: 3.2.0 (GDPR & CCPA Compliant)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview Box -->
      <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Executive Summary:</strong> <span class="font-semibold">freeqrcode-generator.com</span> ("we", "us", "our", or the "Service") is engineered with an uncompromising <em>Privacy-by-Design</em> architecture. Static QR generation operates entirely inside your local web browser without transmitting your payload data to our servers. For Dynamic QR codes and authenticated user workspaces, we implement strict data minimization, zero sale of personal data, and bank-grade cryptographic protections in strict compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), and international privacy frameworks.
      </div>

      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 1. The Zero-Storage Client-Side Generation Principle
        </h2>
        <p>
          Unlike conventional online generators that upload and log your sensitive input values on remote backend servers, <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">freeqrcode-generator.com</strong> processes static QR codes (including Website URLs, Plain Text, Wi-Fi Network SSIDs and Passwords, vCard Contact Profiles, SMS, WhatsApp Messages, UPI Payment strings, and Geo-coordinates) entirely client-side via JavaScript running inside the User's local browser sandbox.
        </p>
        <p>
          Under this zero-storage architecture:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li>Your Wi-Fi passwords, private contact books, and raw messages are never uploaded to, processed by, or cached on our web servers.</li>
          <li>Generating, customizing, and downloading vector SVG or high-resolution PNG QR assets does not create server-side transaction logs containing your payload data.</li>
          <li>If you close your browser tab without saving the code to an authenticated user account, the raw input data immediately ceases to exist outside your local machine.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 2. Categories of Information We Collect
        </h2>
        <p>
          We only collect personal information when strictly necessary to provide authenticated services, facilitate dynamic redirection, or comply with statutory legal obligations.
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-3 pl-2">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">A. Account & Profile Data (Registered Users Only):</h3>
            <p>When you register for a workspace account, we collect your email address, full name, encrypted password hash (derived via salted PBKDF2 with 100,000 iterations), account role, subscription plan tier, and account creation timestamp.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">B. Dynamic QR Codes & Redirection Configuration:</h3>
            <p>When you create Dynamic QR codes or custom mobile landing pages, we store the target destination URL, short code slug identifier, style configuration metadata (hex color codes, frame types, error correction levels), and user account association in our Cloudflare D1 relational database.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">C. Aggregated Dynamic Scan Telemetry (Privacy-Preserving):</h3>
            <p>When an end-user scans a dynamic QR code hosted via our edge router (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/r/:shortCode</code>), our system processes edge metadata to update aggregate analytics for the QR code owner. To preserve end-user privacy:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 pl-4 mt-1">
              <li><strong>Raw IP Addresses are NEVER permanently stored.</strong> IP addresses are processed in volatile memory solely to compute a one-way anonymized cryptographic hash concatenated with a daily salt to identify unique daily scans, after which the raw IP is immediately discarded.</li>
              <li>Geographic data is captured at the country, administrative region, and city level as resolved by Cloudflare edge CDN headers; we do not access precise GPS coordinates.</li>
              <li>Device and browser categories (e.g., iOS Safari, Android Chrome, Windows Desktop) are parsed from the User-Agent header and aggregated into statistical charts.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">D. Billing & Transaction Records:</h3>
            <p>Payment processing for premium subscriptions is handled exclusively by our authorized Merchant of Record (Lemon Squeezy). We do not collect, store, or process raw credit card numbers or bank account credentials on our infrastructure. We retain only the transaction identifier, subscription renewal date, and active plan status.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 3. Legal Grounds for Processing (GDPR Article 6)
        </h2>
        <p>Under the European Union General Data Protection Regulation, we process personal data under the following lawful bases:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Performance of Contract (Art. 6(1)(b)):</strong> Providing registered workspace accounts, dynamic redirection endpoints, and asset storage requested by the user.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate Interests (Art. 6(1)(f)):</strong> Monitoring service uptime, preventing automated spam and malicious phishing campaigns, enforcing our Acceptable Use Policy, and maintaining edge cybersecurity.</li>
          <li><strong>Compliance with Legal Obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)):</strong> Retaining fiscal transaction receipts, fulfilling law enforcement subpoenas, and processing valid DMCA copyright takedown requests.</li>
          <li><strong>Explicit Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)):</strong> Where you have voluntarily opted into direct communication or marketing notifications.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 4. Cookies, Tracking & Local Browser Storage
        </h2>
        <p>
          We employ a minimal, privacy-centric cookie policy:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Essential Session Cookies (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">qr_session</code>):</strong> Strictly necessary HTTP-only, Secure, SameSite=Lax JWT tokens used to authenticate your session when you log into your workspace.</li>
          <li><strong>Local Storage State:</strong> We store your client-side visual theme preference (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">theme: dark/light</code>) and language selection in your browser's <code class="text-xs">localStorage</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Third-Party Advertising Trackers:</strong> We do NOT embed cross-site behavioral tracking beacons, ad network pixels, or third-party data broker scripts. We do NOT sell, rent, or trade your personal data.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 5. Data Subject Rights (GDPR, UK-GDPR & CCPA/CPRA)
        </h2>
        <p>Depending on your geographic residency, you are entitled to exercise statutory data protection rights without financial discrimination:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Right of Access & Portability:</strong> Request a full copy of your account profile, generated QR code records, and scan telemetry in a machine-readable JSON/CSV export format.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Update or correct erroneous account details directly in your Dashboard settings or via support.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure ("Right to be Forgotten"):</strong> Permanently delete your account, saved QR codes, uploaded brand logos, and associated analytics from our database.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Restrict or Object to Processing:</strong> Object to specific data processing operations predicated on legitimate interest.</li>
          <li><strong>California "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information":</strong> We do not sell personal information as defined by the CCPA/CPRA. California residents may submit statutory privacy requests at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To submit a verified data subject request, email our Data Protection Desk at <a href="mailto:privacy@freeqrcode-generator.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-bold underline">privacy@freeqrcode-generator.com</a>. We respond to all verified statutory inquiries within thirty (30) days.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 6. Data Security, Cryptography & Cloudflare Infrastructure
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our application is deployed on Cloudflare’s enterprise serverless edge network (Cloudflare Workers, D1 Database, and R2 Object Storage). All data in transit is encrypted using mandatory Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3 / HTTPS) with HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) headers. Database records and asset buckets are encrypted at rest using AES-256 standards.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 7. Children's Online Privacy Protection (COPPA)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our Service is designed for general audiences and commercial business operators. We do not knowingly solicit, collect, or process personal data from children under the age of thirteen (13) (or sixteen (16) within the European Economic Area). If you believe a minor has established an account without parental consent, please contact us immediately for expedited account termination.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-600"></span> 8. Modifications to this Privacy Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to revise this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect technological advancements, regulatory amendments, or service enhancements. The current revision date will always be prominently displayed at the top of this document. Continued use of freeqrcode-generator.com subsequent to any update constitutes formal acknowledgment of the revised provisions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact Box -->
      <div class="border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-500">
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Legal Contact & Data Protection Officer:</p>
        <p>Free QR Code Generator • Powered by <strong>FK DIGITAL MEDIA</strong></p>
        <p>Support Email: <a href="mailto:support@freeqrcode-generator.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 underline font-semibold">support@freeqrcode-generator.com</a></p>
        <p>Legal & Privacy: <a href="mailto:legal@freeqrcode-generator.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 underline font-semibold">legal@freeqrcode-generator.com</a></p>
        <p>Website: <a href="https://freeqrcode-generator.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 underline">https://freeqrcode-generator.com</a></p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
